# Mutation plan for the four personal-access-token reads (api4/user.go:3080, :3103, :3155, :3188).
#
#   scripts/mutate-batch.sh scripts/mutations/user-access-tokens.plan
#
# Two things carry this family: the **secret** — cleared in the app layer on three of the four
# routes, and `omitempty` so a cleared one is an absent key — and the **permission cascade**,
# which is a different rule on every route and is the only thing between a
# `read_user_access_token` holder and someone else's credentials.
#
# The store's two list queries have no ORDER BY and are not mutated for order: Go has none
# either, and adding one would be the divergence rather than the fix.
#
# **Two mutations survived the first run and both were the same fixture gap in different clothes:**
# no stock role separates the permissions this family distinguishes.
#
#   * `manage_system` and `read_user_access_token` are held together by every role that holds
#     either, so swapping them on `GET /users/tokens` was invisible. A planted role with only the
#     second now asserts the installation-wide routes refuse it.
#   * `SessionHasPermissionToUserOrBot` falls through to the user check on **one** error — the bot
#     store's not-found, from `SqlBotStore.Get` — and must not on any other. Telling those apart
#     needs a caller with `read_others_bots` but not `manage_others_bots` (so the bot path refuses
#     with a *permission* error) **and** `edit_other_users` (so the user path would grant). That is
#     `a_refusal_on_a_bot_does_not_fall_through_to_the_user_check`, and without it a caller could
#     read every bot's access tokens. **That HTTP test was not enough**: over HTTP both answers are
#     the same 403, because the route refuses either way when the caller cannot reach the bot. The
#     two mutations therefore run under `app`, against `db_user_or_bot`, where the function returns
#     a `bool` and the difference is visible. The parity test stays — it is what proves the routes
#     consult the function at all.
#
# The last two lines are the no-op controls and must SURVIVE.

